{#
    Puts the filter button into the row above the product grid - the row that
    already carries sorting, items per page and the grid/list switch.

    This partial is the first thing that row includes and the only one of them
    with a block of its own, so it is the single hook into that row on both the
    search page and a category listing. Neither theme file is touched.

    Only the button. The chips go on their own full-width line above the row,
    from the page templates - there can be a lot of them, and squeezing them
    into a row of controls makes both unreadable.

    The button is placed by flex order rather than by markup position: the
    module's markup has to enter through this one block, which comes first, and
    would otherwise sit in front of the theme's own controls.
#}
{% extends "widget/locator/attributes.html.twig" %}

{% block widget_locator_attributes %}
    {{ parent() }}

    {% include "@foun10EasySearch/frontend/toolbar.html.twig" %}
{% endblock %}
